    "updated_at": "2023-01-13T16:34:13Z",
    "body": "There is also the following text prior to the note:\r\n\r\n> If an [HTML document](https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#html-document) does not start with a BOM, and its [encoding](https://encoding.spec.whatwg.org/#encoding) is not explicitly given by [Content-Type metadata](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/urls-and-fetching.html#content-type), and the document is not [an iframe srcdoc document](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/iframe-embed-object.html#an-iframe-srcdoc-document), then the encoding must be specified using a [meta](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/semantics.html#the-meta-element) element with a [charset](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/semantics.html#attr-meta-charset) attribute or a [meta](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/semantics.html#the-meta-element) element with an [http-equiv](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/semantics.html#attr-meta-http-equiv) attribute in the [Encoding declaration state](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/semantics.html#attr-meta-http-equiv-content-type).\r\n\r\nPerhaps that could be reworded to say that the character encoding declaration, *if* it is present, should be set with the proper charset or http-equiv attribute.\r\n\r\nThank you for your attention.",
