    "updated_at": "2023-01-14T17:09:18Z",
    "body": "I recently received a notification that brought issue #5461 to my attention. That issue regards distinguishing between author and implementation requirements, such as the requirements on `<meta charset>` elements. Although I can't seem to find the original comment that mentioned it, I agree that the issue is relevant to this one, and it seems that addressing it would entail a clear distinction in [the section on character encoding declarations](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/semantics.html#charset) between what is required of authors and what is required of implementations. That seems to be the source of my confusion. Therefore, I've decided to close this issue. Thanks to @domenic, @pshaughn and others who have helped me to learn and better understand web specifications.",
